Title: 0002-sdl2-software-renderer-aros
Repository: grafx2
Base-Commit: f84cb09dc59d706d6e7b28778b01ba911f52298c
Requires: 0001-png-stdio-callbacks.patch
Author: aros-grafx2 project
Date: 2026-09-20
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: AROS software preference; NULL guards are generic SDL2.

Problem:
  First ABIv11 run crashed in stdlib memremove during GFX2_UpdateRect (SDL_LockTexture path) after SDL_CreateRenderer ACCELERATED|VSYNC succeeded. No NULL checks.
Solution:
  On AROS, create a software renderer first (GrafX2 already paints in software). Keep a generic accelerated-then-software fallback elsewhere. Guard NULL window/renderer/texture/surface before update.
Validation:
  2026-09-20 AROS One x86_64 ABIv11 under QEMU: after this patch GrafX2 2.9
  opened with skins and no memremove requester. Evidence:
  docs/attachments/2026-09-20-abiv11-launch/retry-software.png.
  Patch 0007 later drops the sticky software hint around the accelerated
  fallback; that path has not been shown to work on AROS.
Removal:
  Keep the AROS software-first CreateRenderer until an accelerated renderer
  survives GFX2_UpdateRect. NULL guards are generic.

diff --git a/src/sdlscreen.c b/src/sdlscreen.c
index 8acf20a1..64cf618a 100644
--- a/src/sdlscreen.c
+++ b/src/sdlscreen.c
@@ -120,6 +120,35 @@ void Screen_FillRect(int x, int y, int w, int h, byte color)
 #if defined(USE_SDL2)
 // used in GFX2_Set_mode() and GFX2_UpdateScreen()
 static SDL_Rect render_dstrect;
+
+/// Prefer an accelerated vsync renderer; fall back to software.
+/// AROS SDL2 has previously returned a renderer that then crashes in
+/// texture upload (GFX2_UpdateRect -> memremove). Software is enough:
+/// GrafX2 already draws into its own 8-bit surface.
+static SDL_Renderer *GFX2_CreateRenderer(SDL_Window *window)
+{
+  SDL_Renderer *renderer;
+
+#if defined(__AROS__)
+  // AROS SDL2 can return a non-NULL accelerated renderer that then dies in
+  // SDL_LockTexture / stdlib memremove on the first GFX2_UpdateRect.
+  // GrafX2 already renders in software; present through SDL's software path.
+  SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER, "software");
+  renderer = SDL_CreateRenderer(window, -1, SDL_RENDERER_SOFTWARE);
+  if (renderer != NULL)
+    return renderer;
+  GFX2_Log(GFX2_WARNING, "software SDL renderer failed (%s), trying default\n", SDL_GetError());
+#endif
+  renderer = SDL_CreateRenderer(window, -1, SDL_RENDERER_ACCELERATED | SDL_RENDERER_PRESENTVSYNC);
+  if (renderer != NULL)
+    return renderer;
+  GFX2_Log(GFX2_WARNING, "accelerated SDL renderer failed (%s), trying software\n", SDL_GetError());
+  SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER, "software");
+  renderer = SDL_CreateRenderer(window, -1, SDL_RENDERER_SOFTWARE);
+  if (renderer == NULL)
+    GFX2_Log(GFX2_ERROR, "software SDL renderer failed: %s\n", SDL_GetError());
+  return renderer;
+}
 #endif
 
